WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:04.410
- [Interviewer] Okay,
Ryley, Ryley, welcome back.

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:05.243
- Hello.

00:00:05.243 --> 00:00:06.076
- [Interviewer] How you been?

00:00:06.076 --> 00:00:07.487
It's been six, seven months
since we talked to you.

00:00:07.487 --> 00:00:09.290
- [Ryley] I think it's been nine.

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:10.160
No.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.070
- [Interviewer] It was last summer.

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:12.270
- [Ryley] It's been eight.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:13.130
- [Interviewer] Yeah,
probably around that.

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:15.130
- [Ryley] April. March, April.

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:16.320
- [Interviewer] I really
enjoyed your last talk.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.300
'Cause you're so
well-spoken, so intelligent.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.040
You speak so beautifully
about what you've been through

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.770
and what you're going through.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.190
Well, tell me what's going on, now.

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:25.023
Where you at?

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:31.683
- I suppose, since last time we spoke,

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.640
I've been struggling with
the want or need to get

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:42.640
into treatment or let alone
even get out of Los Angeles.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:44.650
- [Interviewer] You were leaving for rehab

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:46.250
the day we did the last interview.

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:47.130
- I thought I was

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:47.963
(Interviewer laughs)

00:00:47.963 --> 00:00:52.963
But, it turned out the guy I was with,

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:55.400
they pretty much just all lied to me

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.060
so that they could get her into treatment.

00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:01.173
And, I wasn't along for
the ride on that one.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:03.293
So it is what it is.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:07.820
But recently, actually
what's funny is I'm planning

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:10.810
on going to Orange County to
go through a treatment center

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:13.940
down there, as soon as possible really.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:14.903
- [Interviewer] Excellent.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:19.470
You spoke a lot last time

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:21.830
about what your childhood was like

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:25.173
and the abuse you got from your dad.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.920
And the more I've learned since that talk,

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:30.670
that that's everything.

00:01:30.670 --> 00:01:33.633
That's the core where it all stems from.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:36.570
All this abuse, all the drug addiction,

00:01:38.034 --> 00:01:40.490
all the self destruction,
self destruction you see

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:42.773
on my channel kind of stems from that.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.970
I would call it rewiring of your brain

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:49.700
when you get that kind of abuse.

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:50.533
- Right.

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:53.080
- [Interviewer] And then it's almost like

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:54.830
your efforts to do the right thing,

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:01.680
just get turned upside down by
your self destructive nature

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:04.683
and there you are, back
in on the street again.

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:11.180
- Yeah, that's basically
what's been going on lately.

00:02:11.180 --> 00:02:13.630
I moved to North Hollywood for a while

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:17.173
and then recently month and a
half ago, I moved back here,

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:22.710
because I ruined the housing
situation I was in over there.

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:26.590
Like, I had one opportunity to take

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:28.560
from somebody that I shouldn't have

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:29.750
and I fucking did it.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:33.150
Like, I took the chance,
you know what I mean?

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:35.940
I weighed my options and I took the chance

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:37.560
and they knew immediately it was me

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:40.390
because I'm not gonna lie
about it when I'm confronted.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:42.910
And like I was like, yeah, I did that.

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:44.990
And that's how it's been for me.

00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:47.350
I'll go like two months, three months,

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:50.300
everything good make the right choices

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.760
and then I'll make one wrong decision.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:56.993
And my consequences are
bad, usually very bad.

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:02.790
- [Interviewer] Is stealing in your nature

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:06.303
or is it just the drugs that
make you do this kind of stuff?

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:12.220
- It's the lack of finances
lately in the last eight weeks,

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:14.750
I haven't been had any access

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:18.080
to my money through unemployment.

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:21.060
Because they canceled my card
and I've been having troubles

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:23.560
getting it back in the
mail for some reason.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:27.927
So that lack of any money
to survive at all has,

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:32.913
which I've been at in the past.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:37.540
It's just been like
crucial, like fucked up.

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:40.400
Like I can't, it's, I've
almost died because of this,

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.310
'cause I have no money.

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:42.570
You know what I mean?

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:43.770
And I don't like to steal

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:46.810
but when I see an
opportunity to do something

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:50.490
where I can make money for survival,

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:51.460
for the drugs that I need,

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:53.660
for the food I need,
for the housing I need.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:57.163
Sometimes I take that chance.

00:03:58.610 --> 00:04:01.030
- [Interviewer] And last
time you were using heroin?

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:02.020
- Right.

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:03.530
- [Interviewer] Is that continued?

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:05.903
- I still sometimes do.

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:11.390
Within the last month I've
started using fentanyl.

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:12.563
I started smoking it.

00:04:14.636 --> 00:04:17.233
I don't know how much
better or worse that is.

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:22.623
'Cause I smoked that and
I don't shoot it but,

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:27.370
it's much more strong and it

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:30.620
when I don't have it, I feel even worse

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:34.023
and it's scaring me.

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:38.723
The progression of it,
is really scaring me.

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:43.830
And I just, that's what's
pushing me to quit right now,

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:44.780
to go to rehab again.

00:04:44.780 --> 00:04:49.043
Because, I know if I
continue with the fentanyl,

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:51.940
it's gonna get really bad, really quick.

00:04:53.470 --> 00:04:55.400
And pretty soon when I don't have it,

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:57.700
I'm not gonna be able to move,

00:04:57.700 --> 00:04:59.300
which is a scary place to be in.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:02.387
I don't want nothing
controlling me like that.

00:05:02.387 --> 00:05:04.590
- [Interviewer] And you're
intelligent enough to know better

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:06.843
but it's not about intelligence here is?

00:05:09.041 --> 00:05:09.960
- It never was.

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:12.820
- [Interviewer] Tell me
about drug addiction from-

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:14.180
- From my standpoint?

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:16.333
- [Interviewer] It's such a-

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:19.263
- It's a conniving thing.

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:21.740
It doesn't matter if you're the smartest

00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:23.103
or dumbest person on earth,

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:27.210
you can be the smartest person on earth

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:30.470
and have no addiction in your family

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:34.130
and have a good upbringing
and do heroin 10 times

00:05:34.130 --> 00:05:35.163
and not be addicted.

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:38.740
Or you could have the same situations

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:40.830
and do it once and become addicted.

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:42.840
So it's really fucking confusing.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:44.163
It doesn't make any sense.

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:48.580
I think everyone's just different

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:51.250
and our brains are wired differently.

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:55.360
And sometimes we use
is, we'll use something

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:58.823
and we'll discover it to
be a crutch very quickly.

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:02.600
And, I think that's that
determining factor of

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:05.793
whether or not we become addicts or not.

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:09.230
It's, I think the environment
has a lot more to do

00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:12.183
with it now than I ever thought before.

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:14.730
- [Interviewer] Environment being like,

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:15.860
your current environment or-

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:16.980
- Surroundings. Yeah.

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:18.753
Like this city, for instance,

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:24.300
even famous people do
like methamphetamine.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:26.740
It's like normal, people are used to it.

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:27.573
It's okay.

00:06:28.507 --> 00:06:30.940
You know, I thought that
was really funny and weird.

00:06:30.940 --> 00:06:32.690
But I found that out one night

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:37.420
because it's a very
popular drug in the city.

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:39.273
- [Interviewer] Crystal meth?

00:06:39.273 --> 00:06:40.106
- Right.
- Yeah.

00:06:40.106 --> 00:06:42.450
- It's not so much cocaine
anymore, like it was.

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:46.430
It's more crystal meth and I've realized

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:50.260
that I'm not so much, I'm not
doing that as much anymore

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:54.890
because, I feel weird on it.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:56.990
There's gotta be something else in it that

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:00.150
just doesn't make me feel right.

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:02.943
- [Interviewer] What did the
crystal meth do it for you?

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:08.960
- Well, I've been tested
on a, like a 16 panel test

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:12.760
after I know that I've just
been using heroin and meth

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:16.583
and I've popped for five
different drugs, like MDMA.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:20.603
I don't even remember.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:24.840
I don't even remember, but
there was two hallucinogenics

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:29.710
and then PCP, methamphetamine
and amphetamine

00:07:29.710 --> 00:07:32.040
and that's just from the meth.

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:33.480
And so if that's what's in there

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:36.740
like why would I wanna introduce
that to my body anymore?

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:37.750
- [Interviewer] I'm not
sure you know exactly

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:39.050
what you're buying on the street anyway?

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:40.300
- No.

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:42.750
No, and I'm not sure I
should be doing that anyways.

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:43.753
- [Interviewer] That's right.

00:07:47.549 --> 00:07:49.117
- It's just it's, yeah.

00:07:49.117 --> 00:07:50.260
- [Interviewer] Do you think if you went

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:51.830
to this Orange County rehab

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:57.470
and somehow got clean or
gotten a much better place

00:07:57.470 --> 00:07:59.720
where you using a lot less perhaps

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:01.033
with Suboxone or whatever,

00:08:03.630 --> 00:08:05.780
that that in combination with some therapy

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:08.330
to work out what you
went through as a child,

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:09.850
might get you to a point

00:08:09.850 --> 00:08:12.593
where you're not so prone to a reuse?

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:15.760
- Well, I'll be honest here,

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:20.750
I think it all came down to
my relationship with my ex

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:25.720
and my son and that whole catastrophe

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:29.063
is what kept me sick for so long.

00:08:29.930 --> 00:08:33.793
I think now that she made
it so we're separated,

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:37.690
I finally had the chance
to think about myself

00:08:37.690 --> 00:08:41.030
and actually, if I'm going to go to rehab

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:44.730
and have the ability to think
about myself and only that,

00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:45.860
because I'm not gonna be worried

00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:47.760
about a relationship I no longer have,

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:49.993
if that makes sense?

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:53.090
At this point, I'm just worried about

00:08:57.104 --> 00:08:59.050
being a part of my son's life,

00:09:01.577 --> 00:09:05.120
you know, because she's
gotten custody back

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:07.670
within the last month
'cause she's been clean

00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:10.423
for a month or a year and two months.

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:13.380
And so now I have this opportunity

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:18.380
where I can selfishly do it
and it might actually work.

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:22.450
And that's a scary thing for me.

00:09:22.450 --> 00:09:24.500
So at the same time, I don't wanna do it.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:29.043
Which doesn't make any sense either, but.

00:09:30.501 --> 00:09:32.273
- [Interviewer] The
life you're living now,

00:09:32.273 --> 00:09:33.470
